ect.buyer_actions (Required): Array of {@see BuyerActionInput}. What the buyer can do with the subscription, in this order: cancel, pause, resume, reactivate, update_payment_method, retry_payment, update_delivery, skip, update_billing_interval, update_quantity, swap_items, change_plan, cancel_plan_change, then renew, under the store's buyer policy. The available cancel and pause actions carry the choices they accept. A buyer's read or change through a customer session on /v1/me, or in Flint's buyer account, lists all fourteen every time; a merchant read gets an empty list. update_payment_method is required while a payment is past due, due by next_retry_at when a retry is scheduled, and when the card expires before next_billing_at, due by then. Example: []. object.buyer_actions[] (Value): {@see BuyerActionInput}. One thing a buyer can do with an order, subscription, invoice or return they read through /v1/me. Show the actions with is_required as what needs the buyer's attention, and the first available action as the primary action on the resource's page in your account. object.cancel_at_period_end (Required): boolean. True when the subscription is scheduled to cancel at scheduled_cancel_at. Schedule with POST /v1/subscriptions/{subscription_id}/cancel; undo with PATCH and cancel_at_period_end false. object.canceled_at (Optional): string. RFC3339 timestamp. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.cancellation_details (Optional): {@see SubscriptionCancellationDetailsInput}. Who asked to cancel, when, and why. Present once a cancellation is requested, whether it takes effect at the end of the billing period or right away. Omitted when no one asked, and removed when a scheduled cancellation is undone. See cancellation_reason for voluntary and payment-related cancellations. The cancellation request behind a scheduled or completed cancellation. object.cancellation_reason (Optional): string. Why the subscription is canceled or scheduled to cancel. Uses end_after_reached when the automatic ending agreement is reached, cancellation_details.requested_by when recorded, payment_failed for other canceled subscriptions without a requester, and other for a scheduled cancellation without a requester. Omitted otherwise. Value enum: "buyer", "merchant", "integration", "payment_failed", "other", "end_after_reached". object.completed_cycles (Required): integer. Billing cycles charged so far, including cycles imported with `billing_start.completed_cycles`. The next renewal order's `subscription_cycle` is this number plus one. Format: uint64. minimum: 0. object.contract_end_at (Optional): string. When the recorded contract term ends. Does not move when the subscription pauses or changes plan. Flint does not stop the buyer from canceling earlier. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.contract_start_at (Optional): string. When the recorded contract term started. Does not move when the subscription pauses or changes plan. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.created_at (Required): string. RFC3339 timestamp. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.current_period_end_at (Optional): string. RFC3339 timestamp. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.current_period_start_at (Optional): string. RFC3339 timestamp. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.customer (Optional): {@see ExpandedCustomerSummaryInput} or null. Present only when `expand` includes `customer`; `null` when expanded and there is no related customer. object.customer.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see ExpandedCustomerSummaryInput}. A customer's summary fields, returned in place of a customer ID when the customer is expanded. object.customer.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.customer_id (Required): string. The customer this subscription bills. Example: "cus_01KEZF7C006X9JK6NZNA2SM9XD". object.delivery (Optional): {@see SubscriptionDeliveryInput}. Saved delivery preference with the current delivery method display. Write responses use the same display as GET: fixed shipping reflects the current method configuration, and quoted shipping shows the last paid shipping amount when available. A subscription's saved delivery preference: method, destination, recipient, shipping cost, and who last changed it. object.delivery_hold (Optional): {@see SubscriptionDeliveryHoldInput}. Current delivery issue that blocks collection. Mutually exclusive with upcoming_delivery_hold. A hold on a subscription's deliveries because its delivery method or destination no longer works, and who can fix it. object.early_termination_fee_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput}. The fee in the recorded contract terms. Present whenever those terms include a fee. It applies only to a cancellation before contract_end_at. Flint never charges it. Later plan changes do not change this fee. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.end_after (Required): {@see SubscriptionEndAfterInput} or null. Recorded automatic end condition. Null when no automatic end is set. Cycles count charged billing periods, including imported completed_cycles. Pauses and skips do not use cycles. Already-paid prepaid deliveries continue on their shifted dates, even beyond the end date, and cancellation waits for the last remaining delivery. Skipping defers a delivery without consuming its entitlement. Ending never refunds. object.end_after.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see SubscriptionEndAfterInput}. The subscription's automatic end condition, measured by charged billing cycles or a saved local calendar date. object.end_after.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.expires_at (Required): string or null. Projected end under the current schedule and committed plan changes, including an earlier scheduled cancellation. A date limit preserves already-paid entitlement without requiring a future charge schedule. A reached cycle limit uses the last paid period end, or current_period_end_at when