th flint_ are reserved for Flint and are not returned. Writes follow the limits on MetadataInput and MetadataPatchInput; maps written before those limits may not satisfy them. object.missed_billing_at (Optional): string. The billing date whose payment failed, as an RFC3339 timestamp. Present only while status is past_due. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.next_billing_at (Optional): string. When Flint next starts a scheduled renewal charge, as an RFC3339 timestamp. Present only while a trialing or active subscription has a billing date and isn't set to cancel at the end of its period. Absent when no renewal is scheduled: a paused subscription resumes at scheduled_resume_at, a past_due one reports the failed billing date in missed_billing_at and retries at next_retry_at, an incomplete one retries at next_retry_at, a scheduled start begins at starts_at, one set to cancel ends at scheduled_cancel_at, and an external schedule awaiting a date reports is_awaiting_billing_schedule. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.next_retry_at (Required): string or null. Recorded automatic payment retry time. Null when no retry time is available. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.open_renewal_order_id (Optional): string. ID of the paid renewal order whose shipment has not been dispatched. It keeps its committed delivery destination after preference changes and cancellation. Absent when no such renewal order exists. Only renewal orders count; the signup order is not included. Example: "ord_01KEZF7C0054GQKJ142A8X367A". object.outstanding_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput}. Unpaid balance of the failed renewal order, including tax, shipping and discounts, after payments and credits. Present only while status is past_due and a positive balance remains. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.pause_reason (Optional): string. Why the subscription is paused: merchant for a pause made with your API key or dashboard, buyer for the buyer's own pause, delivery_action_required for a pause during or after a delivery hold, and payment_failed when renewal payment retries ran out and your dunning settings pause the subscription. Omitted when the subscription is not paused. Value enum: "buyer", "delivery_action_required", "merchant", "payment_failed". object.paused_at (Optional): string. RFC3339 timestamp. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.payment_method (Optional): {@see ExpandedPaymentMethodSummaryInput} or null. Present only when `expand` includes `payment_method`; `null` when expanded and there is no related payment method. object.payment_method.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see ExpandedPaymentMethodSummaryInput}. A payment method's summary fields, including type, status, and card details, returned when the payment method is expanded. object.payment_method.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.payment_method_due_at (Required): string or null. First charge boundary while no card is bound: the later of trial_end_at and next_billing_at during a trial, or the next billing date for an imported period, even when that cycle's charge is zero. Recomputed when the schedule changes. A trial still without a card at its boundary cancels without an order or payment attempt. At that boundary, an imported subscription with a positive charge that still has no card enters its normal dunning schedule without a payment attempt. For an imported subscription, a zero charge completes the renewal without a card and the deadline advances to the following boundary. Null when a card is bound, collection is not scheduled (paused, canceled, or set to cancel at period end), or an external schedule has no known boundary. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.payment_method_id (Required): string or null. Saved payment method used for renewal charges. Null when no card is bound. Bind a card to this subscription with PATCH; changing the 